 "answer": "The earliest 2024 paper in the index is **“Large Language Model based Multi-Agents: A Survey of Progress and Challenges”** (arXiv:2402.01680), with an indexed publication date of **January 21, 2024**. [D1]\n\n- **Main idea:** It surveys systems where multiple LLM-powered agents—with different roles and skills—communicate and collaborate, rather than relying on a single agent. [C1][C2]\n- **What it covers:** Four design dimensions: interaction with the environment, agent roles, communication and collaboration, and how agents acquire capabilities. [C4]\n- **Applications:** It groups work into **problem-solving** and **world simulation**, with examples including software development, multi-robot systems, and simulations of societies, policies, and games. [C3][C4]\n- **Main contribution:** A structured map of the field, alongside implementation frameworks, datasets, benchmarks, and discussion of research challenges—not a new standalone agent system. [C1][C4]",
